{
	"name": "Death Potion",
	"type": "object",
	"img": "icons/magic/death/grave-tombstone-glow-teal.webp",
	"system": {
		"description": "<p>Anyone using one of your potions can apply it to a weapon or food as a bonus action. Applying a potion to an unwilling target requires you to grapple with, or successfully grab on, your target, but allows you to use an action to force-feed the target on a failed Constitution save.</p><p>A creature that willingly drinks this potion, aware of its effects, dies with no saving throws. A creature unaware of the potion’s nature must make a Constitution saving throw. On a successful save, they instead take 6d10 necrotic damage. If this damage would reduce them to 0 HP they become [[/condition id=doomed]].</p>",
